# Keys whose signatures let CI skip reproducing an experiment record (openinterp sign).
# One signer per line, in OpenSSH allowed_signers format:
#   <principal> valid-after="YYYYMMDDZ",namespaces="openinterp-record" <key type> <public key>
# CI reads this file from the pull request's base branch, so a pull request can't add
# its own key: a new signer has to land on main first.
# Each signature is checked at the time it landed on main, against its key's window.
# valid-after is the UTC day the key was added. To revoke a key, don't delete its line:
# add valid-before="YYYYMMDDHHMMSSZ" at the start of its exposure (SECURITY.md).
8W9aG valid-after="20261019Z",namespaces="openinterp-record" ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIIqEox4VWoOevD6XjbEL/deUlohM5pbqy25SDbKZJIxD openinterp record signing (8W9aG)
8W9aG valid-after="20261028Z",namespaces="openinterp-record" ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIBkANRLBF0s5MrNdD2sPrxTbhGi7ipXpOzyquRVUiqt3 openinterp record signing (8W9aG, linux)
